==Fast foods==
{{main|Food/Fast foods}}
Fast foods refer to a subtype of food that incur non-standard attack or eating delays when they are consumed. This means you may be able to eat them faster, or attack more quickly after eating one than you could with other foods.
*For comparison with the chart below, most foods add a 3-tick (1.8 second) penalty to when a player may attack, or eat again.

===Combo eating===
Combo eating is a strategy that allows the healing effect from multiple foods to apply in a single server tick. The most common example involves eating a [[cooked karambwan]] or [[halibut]] directly after eating another non-combo food. This consumes both foods and applies healing instantly.
{{Fast_foods_table}}

==Hunter meats==
Hunter meats, when eaten, will heal an initial amount before doing so again after 7 ticks (4.2 seconds), making it heal more Hitpoints overall than other foods in its level bracket. If a second hunter meat is eaten before the effect happens, only the most recent secondary heal will occur. The secondary effect will not be cancelled when eating other foods such as [[manta ray]]s or [[cooked karambwan]]s, however.

By default, players with the appropriate [[Cooking]] level can cook low tier hunter meat, but higher quality meats require having completed a set amount of [[Hunters' Rumours]] before being able to cook them.
{{Hunter meats table}}

== Inventory-blocking foods ==
{{Main|Inventory_blocking_food}}
Some foods leave behind an item in the [[inventory]] after being consumed. They are commonly used while fighting the [[Chaos Elemental]], [[Chaos Fanatic]], and [[blackjacking]] in [[Pollnivneach]].

==Niche foods==
These foods can be more useful than the more commonly used foods, but will usually only see use in more niche scenarios due to their high cost, low trade volume, difficulty to obtain, or limited use cases. Some uses would include speed, endurance, or low-level challenges for various bosses, supplementing other food as a means to perform specific strategies, or [[Ironman mode|Ironmen]] who do not wish to train Cooking very high.
